      "essence": "Sincere restraint preserves correct position until responsibility, timing, and conditions can support consequential action.",
      "summary": "The Confucian lens treats Waiting as disciplined conduct under conditions that are not yet ready for advance. Sincerity and steadfastness keep strength from becoming rash, while centrality and correctness preserve one’s place within the larger order. The Image adds a cultivated ease: nourishment and composure are not evasions of duty but ways of remaining fit for it. The line sequence distinguishes distance from danger, increasing exposure, and the balanced authority able to wait without losing purpose. Action becomes appropriate when timing, position, and responsibility align, so restraint and progress belong to one continuous practice.",
