      "essence": "Gate 5 describes Sacral consistency within natural rhythms, while full meaning still depends on activation and chart context.",
      "summary": "Within Human Design, Gate 5 concerns fixed rhythms: the Sacral capacity to sustain recurring patterns and wait within a natural tempo. Its harmonic relationship with Gate 15 forms the 15–5 Channel of Rhythm in the Understanding Circuit, but a static Gate description does not establish that channel or any personal activation. The source frames waiting as active attunement rather than vacant delay, with pressure arising when concepts try to alter an embodied pattern. Differentiated expression appears as steadiness within timing, while distortion appears as identification with imposed routines or impatience toward the unexpected. Line, planetary, and chart context remain necessary for a complete reading.",
