      "essence": "Impatience softens into patient participation in life’s rhythms, opening contemplation beyond the pressure of measured time.",
      "summary": "The Gene Keys lens names the movement of Key 5 as a passage from Impatience through Patience toward Timelessness. Its constricted pattern appears when distrust of timing turns natural rhythm into pressure, making the present feel like an obstacle to what should already have arrived. Patience is described less as passive endurance than as growing sensitivity to recurring patterns that cannot be hurried without distortion. As awareness releases its demand for immediate resolution, time can be experienced as participation rather than scarcity. Timelessness marks the system’s highest contemplative horizon, not a guaranteed attainment or a claim about anyone’s present state.",
